hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition modeling the masters I  believe that the fastest and most  effective way to grow your business is  to model the strategies of people who  have already done what you're trying to  do so today we're going to look at how  three young men who were all coming from  humble beginnings decided to come  together launch a business which became  one of the most successful and popular  websites in the world this is a story of  the founders of Twitter and a top three  lessons and you can learn from their  success Jack Dorsey Christopher Isaac  biz stone and Evan Williams were all on  different career paths when they met and  created one of the world's most prolific  social media sites Twitter in 2000  Dorsey started an online company to  dispatch couriers taxis and emergency  workers this work would soon evolved  into an idea for real-time status  communication stones entrepreneurial  spirit showed at a young age when he  founded a lacrosse team in high school  and coordinated a senior play after the  school decided to cancel it in 1999 a  friend of stones pitched him an idea for  a new company called xanga comm which  they launched together but in less than  a year stone had grown frustrated with  the direction of xanga and moved to Los  Angeles where he worked in television  for a while and wrote a book on blogging  Williams grew up on a farm far from the  high-tech lifestyle he would later  embrace where summers friend you're  getting crops he drifted from working on  the family farm to job to several IT  startups in Texas but finally moved to  Sonoma County California to work with  the technology publishing company  O'Reilly Media all three men were at a  crossroad in their lives and it was at  this crossroad that the three budding  entrepreneurs would come together to  make history both Williams and stone are  working for a new Internet company  called bloggers but eventually sold it  to Google and with those stock options  Williams and stone sold out to start  their own company with that o do a  podcast company was born in late 2006  William stone and several OD employees  form obvious corporation while deal was  acquired by sonic mountain one is one of  obvious his first projects was Twitter  Dorsey was also nearly fascinated with  instant  Bastien approached the company to see if  there was room for his collaboration the  team began a day-long brainstorming  session where Dorsey proposed the idea  of using an SMS service to communicate  with a small group of people within just  two weeks Dorson stone had created  prototype of Twitter total is launched  has his own company in April 2007 with  Dorsia CEO Dorsey sought the young  company through two rounds of venture  capital funding in 2008 Williamson would  become CEO of Twitter with Dorsey taking  a role of chairman of the board although  criticized for lack of a business model  by February 2009 Twitter had become the  third most used online social network  with over 55 million monthly visits the  trio had not designed Twitter to earn  money and for the moment were happy  spending their time and energy on  improving the service rather than  turning a profit namely by focusing on  simplicity constraint and craftsmanship  Twitter meanwhile has grown from being  as a social networking site to important  news distribution tool that gets  listened to around the world people are  no longer using it just to update  friends on their meals of the day  Twitter's popularity spiked for instance  during the Iranian elections with news  of events being reported on site before  mainstream media found out the US  government even asked a company to  postpone a 90-minute scheduled  maintenance outage journey elections in  order to ensure people could continue to  use it to share updates today Twitter is  one of the most widely used daily sites  where people around the world including  the President of the United States by  starting small and by taking steps every  day to grow their business the Twitter  founders were able to go from having a  working demo made in two weeks to  building one of the most successful  websites in the world to help you expand  your business  here are three auction items you can  learn from the Twitter guys  action I'm number one choose  collaboration over competition those the  last time you partner with your  competition might sound like a strange  concept but there's sometimes  opportunities to be had by collaborating  with them as an entrepreneur should be  the best at what you do even if it's  only in a very limited area it means  that for some clients you're the best  option and for others might not be you  might create referral opportunities with  competitors you respect who have a  slightly different skill set I might  also open up chances to bid on projects  together to line the client which either  one of you could get on your own keep an  open mind to collaborating with your  competitors the cofounders of Twitter  have taken a unique approach to their  operations they're choosing  collaboration over competition the  promotion of open information exchange  where it might have once been blocked  and instilling that culture throughout  the company Twitter also worked with  some of the industry's heavy hitters  when it came under attack from hackers  early on Stone likes to call it  nourishing the ecosystem and believes  Twitter has a role to play in  facilitating the open exchange of  information in all its forms the  cofounders believed that collaborating  with a competition will help everyone  out this concept is not unique to the  business world but has continued to work  for Twitter according to Dorsey Stone  and Williams there's a lot we can learn  from smart people out in the world  previous companies I've left before I  left I left because I didn't really like  where the culture was going and I wanted  to leave I was too young to realize that  I could have an impact on changing it if  I didn't like it I could work harder I  think a lot of folks are just wired that  way it's product a or product be like  those blind taste tests there's  something healthy about friendly  competition it's like a scrimmage or  pickup game that's good but the truth of  it is that we're all working together  it's like Coke versus Pepsi I notice the  other day that they're following each  other on Twitter actually I'm number two  make it fun starting running a business  is going to be one of the hardest most  challenging things you ever do in your  life so you might as well have some fun  doing it if you're going to work every  day hating it  you need to change things up find a way  to make it more fun and you not only  enjoy it more you get better results  from it as well from the beginning the  co-founders approached  honey a little differently than most  they didn't know how they're going to  make a profit from it and they weren't  sure exactly who would use it but what  they did know was that they liked using  it today despite the popularity to the  service and the near you know celebrity  status of its founders the three  entrepreneurs have managed to keep  themselves in check why because they're  just having fun  still they continue to enjoy all that  their business is brought them including  a new vocabulary the co-founders found  it funny that some of the words accrued  have made it into the official  dictionary according to the founders  early on someone said Twitter is fun but  it isn't useful I've said neither is ice  cream so what if it's just fun we're  working out odyo but we weren't as  passionate about the podcast and service  as we should have been we weren't using  it and that was a problem  Twitter got started because F give us  some freedom to think along different  lines there are different ways to  approach a startup one thing I admired  about Google is we said this thing is  huge and we're going to kick ass at it  people ask how big is a market for  blogging I said I don't know but if we  make it awesome lots of people would do  it with Twitter there is no market other  than we knew it was cool action I'm  number three key in on culture once you  start building beyond yourself you're  going to have to start thinking about  the culture that you want to create at  your company what is your company  staying for and what values do you want  embody you have an opportunity to hire  people who share those values and you  can create that culture from the  beginning if you don't create it  yourself a culture will naturally form  on its own and might not reflect the  direction you wanted to take so plan  accordingly  Dorsey stone and Williams of trying to  build Twitter into more than just a  microblogging service but into a  superorganism into a company that  cultivates a healthy work environment  and culture as much as it does  technological innovation the Twitter  office itself was even designed to  cultivate an open and fun work  environment there are brick walls high  ceilings and no cubicles employees work  side by side at their stations on modern  furniture breakfast is catered with  everything from soy yogurt to fresh  strawberries then comes lunch also  catered for employees including soups  salads and sandwiches  Thursday at Twitter headquarters is a  particularly special day where a guest  speaker anywhere from a businessman to a  musician jonesing for lunch  employees are then encouraged to tweet  about the lunch as it happens based on  their own personal experiences from  working out other company's Twitter  co-founders decided to place a heavy  emphasis on making sure that theirs was  a company people wanted to go to work  for every day according to the founders  he was very genuinely wants to innovate  not just from a product or  technologically sent according to stone  when thinking about Williams he very  genuinely wants to innovate not just him  a product of technology standpoint but  from a company standpoint for me I've  learned about what it means to focus on  a culture to build social responsibility  and the idea of a company is a  superorganism we focus a lot on culture  specifically we don't want to end up  like that child actor who found success  early and grew up all weird and freaky  we want to remain okay just because we  found success early and in many ways got  lucky doesn't mean we're a bunch of  geniuses it means what it means  so remember choose collaboration over  competition make it fun and key in on  culture to finish up this video I wanted  to share with my favorite true stories  about the Twitter guys and some of the  most inspirational quotes Buddha's been  used by everyday people to report  incidents around the world these  remarkable events have been picked up by  news agencies and reported through local  broadcasts and channels while Dorsey  stone and Williams never thought their  technological innovation would become a  major way of reporting instant news  stories they do joke about sitting  around thinking of new words to describe  the creation after brainstorming they  came up with the name Twitter but also  called the process of delivering  real-time information sending a tweet or  tweeting the inside joke according to  Dorsey is that these two made-up words  are now in the newest official English  dictionary Stone said we never believed  these made-up words that we thought were  just funny ways to describe our  invention would become actual English  words found in a dictionary  you  you  you  you  I  thank you for joining me for another  edition Melina masters if you like the  video and you want to see more please  give it a thumbs up below I'd also love  to hear oh you have to think if you want  to leave a comment under the video I  always read those and try to respond  everybody so thank you and we'll see you  on the next episode  you
 

